Subject: [PATCH] Accept legacy widget state without optional Samsung bundles

One UI 9 tries the required Base64 accessor even when older widget state has no
semColorfulInfo/semMonotoneInfo attributes. Check presence before decoding.
Keep absent bundles untouched and retain strict parsing, corruption logging
and Parcel cleanup for present data. No persisted widget data is removed.

diff --git a/smali/com/android/server/appwidget/AppWidgetXmlUtil.smali b/smali/com/android/server/appwidget/AppWidgetXmlUtil.smali
--- a/smali/com/android/server/appwidget/AppWidgetXmlUtil.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/server/appwidget/AppWidgetXmlUtil.smali
@@ -261,6 +261,12 @@
     const/4 v1, 0x0
 
     :try_start_0
+    invoke-interface {p0, v1, p1}, Lcom/android/modules/utils/TypedXmlPullParser;->getAttributeValue(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;
+
+    move-result-object v2
+
+    if-eqz v2, :cond_3
+
     invoke-interface {p0, v1, p1}, Lcom/android/modules/utils/TypedXmlPullParser;->getAttributeBytesBase64(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)[B
 
     move-result-object p0
